course: dictionary
lesson: 7714
title: Names in context
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A proper noun is the name of one special person, place or thing, and it always starts with a capital letter. Ptolemy is a proper noun: it names one particular person or family, so the words around it show which Ptolemy you mean.
explain: «Cleopatra VII was a queen of Egypt from the Ptolemy family, whose family came from Macedonia in Greece.» The clues are queen, Egypt and family. They tell you Ptolemy here means a royal family of kings, not one scientist.
explain: The same name can mean different things in different lessons. In science, Ptolemy's model said the Earth was at the centre of the universe, and Copernicus's Sun-centred model later replaced it. In history, the Ptolemaic kings ruled Egypt. Always check the subject and the sentence before you decide.
fact: A proper noun is a name, and it starts with a capital letter.
fact: Ptolemy was a Greek scientist who lived in Alexandria in Egypt about 1,900 years ago.
fact: Ptolemy also made famous maps, and he wrote that the Earth was at the centre of the universe.
fact: Ptolemy was also the name of several kings of ancient Egypt, after Alexander the Great.
fact: «Ptolemy's model» means the idea of the Earth at the centre, which was later replaced by Copernicus's Sun-centred model.
exercise: «Ptolemy was a Greek scientist who lived in Alexandria.» Why does Ptolemy start with a capital letter? | It starts every sentence | It is the name of a type of map | *It is the name of one special person | It is a very long word
exercise: Ptolemy's model said the Earth was at the centre of the universe. Which later model replaced it? | A model with the Moon at the centre | A model made of clay | *Copernicus's Sun-centred model | Ptolemy's model again
exercise: «The Ptolemaic kings ruled Egypt after Alexander the Great.» What do the clues Egypt and kings tell you? | Ptolemy here means a school subject | Ptolemy here means a Greek scientist | Ptolemy here means a type of boat | *Ptolemy here means a family of Egyptian rulers
test: «Ptolemy was also the name of several kings of ancient Egypt.» In this sentence, what does Ptolemy name? | *A family of kings of ancient Egypt | A lake in Scotland | A famous football team | A city in Greece
test: Ptolemy the scientist lived in which place? | London | Macedonia | *Alexandria | Glasgow
exam: Which sentence uses Ptolemy correctly as a proper noun? | Ptolemy is a very ptolemy word. | We went to ptolemy on holiday. | *Ptolemy wrote that the Earth was at the centre of the universe. | I read a ptolemy about the stars.
